# archive.org credentials (optional)
#
# Rename this file to  .env  and fill it in to have the app sign in on its
# own. Some archive.org sources — the PlayStation one right now — are only
# served to logged-in accounts.
#
# ARCHIVE_EMAIL=you@example.com
# ARCHIVE_PASSWORD=your-password
#
#
# READ THIS FIRST
#
# The password is stored here in PLAIN TEXT. This SD card is FAT32, which has
# no file permissions, so anyone who takes the card out can read it. Unlike a
# session cookie, a password cannot be revoked by logging out — you would have
# to change it. If you reuse this password anywhere else, that account is
# exposed too.
#
# You do NOT need this file. Without it the app asks for your login once, then
# keeps only the session cookie it gets back (archive_cookies.txt), which
# expires on its own and is revoked the moment you log out in a browser. That
# is the safer setup, and it already avoids retyping on every launch. This
# file only saves you from signing in again on the day the session expires.
#
# Delete .env at any time to stop storing the password; nothing else breaks.
#
# The credentials are sent only to archive.org, over a connection verified
# against the bundled cacert.pem, and never anywhere else.
